Home v3 page, Sent events in place of build records

Home (the Main Page boards on the JusPrin v2 canvas):
- A "JusPrin › Home" bar with Preferences. The shell hides its project
  header while Home is on screen, so the page draws its own.
- The gallery leads with a drop tile listing the formats; the whole page
  still takes a drop. Search and a Recent/Name sort appear from eight
  projects. Open… stays the primary action, New the compact secondary.
- First run is one dashed panel with New and Open…, naming the first
  printer when there is one.
- A printer that is not printing and needs no reconnecting is a one-line
  chip until opened; a printer just added opens as its full card.
- Each card shows when it was last saved ("Today", "Yesterday", "Oct 24")
  beside its name, over the host's status line, which ends in an
  ellipsis when long.
- New tokens with brand guards: component.projectGallery (search width,
  header height) and component.homeHeader (height).

Project status: a card reads Draft, Sent <date>, Printed <date> or
Printing on <printer>. ledger_status, a pure function next to
HomeSnapshot, derives it from the project's Sent events and completed
prints; ProjectAutosave reads them from each listed project's document.
Nothing writes Sent events yet: Send preflight will, once it exists, so
every card outside a running job reads Draft until then.

Manufacturing records:
- Removed BuildRecord, ExportedCopyRecord, deterministic_output_hash, the
  record_build, record_export_copy and record_physical_print tools and
  their handler, ProjectStateDocument's build and copy API, the Internal
  tool exposure only they used, and the Agent page's build and copy
  cards. A build was a slice, which nobody acts on, and nothing in the
  app wrote one. Documents that still hold builds load as before.
- Added SentRecord with add_sent, confirm_delivery and sent, and
  sent_record to build one from a workspace snapshot. A physical print
  now links to its Sent event, and the document refuses one without.
- SetupCommands::display_alias is shared so Home names a filament as the
  sidebar does.

